<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  THE camera mounting pose. Single source of truth, included by both camera
  descriptions so sim and hardware cannot drift apart.

    rx150_gripper_depth_camera.urdf.xacro   sim, Gazebo depth sensor
    rx150_realsense_camera.urdf.xacro       hardware, RealSense driver

  Both bolt their camera link onto rx150/gripper_link with this pose, and both
  mean the same physical point - the camera's own reference origin, which for a
  D435 sits a few cm inside the casing. Measure to that point, not to the
  casing, or fold the casing offset in here.

  ##########################################################################
  THESE ARE PLACEHOLDERS, COPIED FROM AN INVENTED SIM OFFSET. MEASURE THEM.
  ##########################################################################
  Nothing errors when they are wrong. The obstacle map and every detected
  object simply come out shifted and rotated by the same amount, everywhere,
  which reads as a broken pipeline rather than a bad number.

  The datum the measurement starts FROM is marked in sim by the green dot in
  rx150_gripper_depth_camera.urdf.xacro (mount_ref_corner). Check the dot is on
  the right feature before trusting anything measured from it.

  xyz is metres, rpy is radians, both relative to gripper_link.
-->
<robot xmlns:xacro="http://www.ros.org/wiki/xacro">
  <xacro:property name="cam_mount_xyz" value="0.0 0.0 0.065" scope="global"/>
  <xacro:property name="cam_mount_rpy" value="0 0 0"         scope="global"/>
</robot>
